            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Will I ever be a true woman?&quot; An exploration of the experiences of women with vestibulodynia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>818-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/07399332.2015.1103739</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this study we explored the experiences of Norwegian women living with vestibulodynia, a chronic disease affecting young women all over the world. Using a phenomenological approach we conducted in-depth interviews with eight women who had struggled with vestibulodynia for several years. Our findings reveal that their efforts to fulfill their partners' sexual desires as well as their own represented an encompassing ongoing process. In addition, we highlight the interrelationship between the intensity of vulvar pain experienced by individual women and decisions women make about prioritizing their own sexual needs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
